# TMS List block

The TMS List block creates an ordered or unordered list. It is designed to work with TMS List Item blocks inside it.

## Settings sidebar

The settings sidebar has two tabs:

- **Wrapper** — List type and attributes
- **Styles** — List-specific visual appearance

### Wrapper tab

#### List Type
- **Unordered List (ul)** — bulleted list (default)
- **Ordered List (ol)** — numbered list

#### Inner blocks
Add more items using the **+** appender, reorder by dragging, nest other blocks inside items.

#### ARIA Controls
Role options: `directory`, `group`, `listbox`, `menu`, `menubar`, `radiogroup`, `tablist`, `toolbar`, `tree`, `presentation`.

#### Custom Attributes, Identity Controls
Same pattern as other blocks.

### Styles tab

List-specific panels: **List Style Type** (disc, circle, square, decimal, etc.), **List Style Position** (outside/inside), **Custom Marker Image**.

## Example HTML output

```html
<ul id="features-list" class="tmsblocks-list-block tmsblocks-list-block-def789 features" aria-label="Available features">
  <li class="tmsblocks-list-item tmsblocks-list-item-abc123"><span>Unlimited projects</span></li>
  <li class="tmsblocks-list-item tmsblocks-list-item-def456"><span>Priority support</span></li>
  <li class="tmsblocks-list-item tmsblocks-list-item-ghi789"><span>Advanced reporting</span></li>
</ul>
```

## Tips
- **Use unordered lists for grouped information** like features, benefits, or links.
- **Use ordered lists for sequences** like steps, rankings, or instructions.
- **Style the list wrapper for shared spacing** and use item-level styles for per-item customizations.

