# TMS Block (Generic Block)

The TMS Block is the core structural block — a smart, flexible wrapper. You pick the HTML tag, drop any other blocks inside it, and style it however you like.

## Settings sidebar

The settings sidebar has two tabs:

- **Wrapper** — Everything about the HTML element itself
- **Styles** — Visual appearance (see The Styles tab)

### Wrapper tab

#### Element Tag
Choose from semantic tags: `div` (default), `section`, `header`, `footer`, `aside`, `nav`, `main`, `article`, `figure`.

**Tip:** Pick the tag that best describes the *meaning* of the content, not just how it's going to look.

#### ARIA Controls
- **ARIA Label** — A text description for screen readers.
- **Role** — Override the implicit ARIA role (e.g. `banner`, `navigation`, `region`, `alert`, `dialog`).
- **Extra ARIA Attributes** — Add other `aria-*` attributes as key-value pairs.

#### Custom Attributes
`data-*` attributes, `tabindex`, `title`, `download`

#### Identity Controls
- **ID**, **CSS Class**

## Example HTML output

```html
<section id="features" class="tmsblocks-generic-block tmsblocks-generic-block-abc123 features-section"
  aria-label="Product features section" role="region" data-theme="light">
  <h2>What You Get</h2>
  <p>Every plan includes all of the core features…</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Unlimited projects</li>
    <li>Priority support</li>
    <li>Advanced reporting</li>
  </ul>
</section>
```

Auto-generated CSS:
```css
body .tmsblocks-generic-block-abc123 {
  margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 40px; padding: 32px;
  background-color: #f5f5f5; border-radius: 8px;
}
@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
  body .tmsblocks-generic-block-abc123:hover { background-color: #e8e8e8; }
}
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  body .tmsblocks-generic-block-abc123 { margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; padding: 16px; }
}
```

## Tips
- **Pick the right tag.** A card is usually an `article`, a sidebar is usually an `aside`.
- **Use the breakpoint selector early.** Switch to Tablet or Mobile to make sure your design works at every screen size.
- **Nest blocks for complex layouts.** You can put a TMS Block inside another TMS Block.

## Example uses
- a **card container** — an `article` with padding, background, rounded corners, and inner blocks
- a **page section** — a `section` with margin, background, and nested content
- a **sticky header bar** — a `header` with `position: sticky`
- a **responsive grid item** — a `div` with flex or grid properties

