# TMS Dynamic Field block

The TMS Dynamic Field block displays data pulled from the current post, a Query Loop, a Post Context, or a specific post. It's the most flexible way to output dynamic content — post titles, dates, custom fields, taxonomy terms, author info, comment counts, and more.

Unlike the other dynamic-capable blocks, this block is purpose-built for dynamic output. It can display multiple values at once, switch between text/image/link output, and style each item independently.

## Settings sidebar

The settings sidebar has three tabs:

- **Settings** — Field path, item type, separator, and container attributes
- **Item** — Styles for each individual item in the output
- **Container** — Styles for the wrapper element around all items

### Settings tab

#### Quick setup
A preset dropdown lets you configure common field paths in one click — Post Title, Post Date, Categories, Tags, Author Name, Featured Image, and more.

#### Field path
Build a path step by step, choosing from:
- **Post fields** — title, date, modified date, excerpt, content, slug, status, ID
- **Custom fields** — any post meta / ACF field
- **Taxonomy terms** — categories, tags, or custom taxonomy terms
- **Author info** — name, email, bio, URL
- **Comments** — comment count

#### Value options
- **Separator** — Text between multiple values (default: `, `).
- **Empty text** — Fallback when the field has no value.
- **Date format** — Custom PHP date format.
- **Comments text** — Singular/plural labels for comment counts.

#### Post source
- **Current** — The current post (or context from Post Context / Query Loop).
- **Specific** — A specific post you search for and select.

#### Item type
- **Text** — Output as inline or block text. Choose HTML tag: `span`, `div`, `p`, `li`, `h2`–`h4`.
- **Image** — Output as `<img>` tags.
- **URL / Link** — Output as clickable `<a>` tags. Additional link settings control href source, label, and target.

#### Container Wrapper
Collapsible panel with tag, ID, CSS class, ARIA controls, and custom attributes for the container.

### Item tab

Style panels depend on item type:

| Item type | Style panels available |
|---|---|
| **Text** | Typography, Color, Background, Border, Spacing, Dimension, Effects, Display, Position, Flex/Grid Item |
| **Image** | Dimension, Border, Effects, Object (fit/position), Display, Position, Spacing, Flex/Grid Item |
| **URL / Link** | Typography, Color, Background, Border, Spacing, Dimension, Effects, Display, Position, Flex/Grid Item |

### Container tab

Full set of style panels for the wrapper element — same as The Styles tab.

## Example HTML output

```html
<div class="tmsblocks-dynamic-field tmsblocks-dynamic-field-abc789 post-categories">
  <span data-tmsblocks-dynamic-field-item>
    <a href="https://example.com/category/tutorials">Tutorials</a>
  </span>
  <span class="tmsblocks-dynamic-field-separator" aria-hidden="true">, </span>
  <span data-tmsblocks-dynamic-field-item>
    <a href="https://example.com/category/wordpress">WordPress</a>
  </span>
</div>
```

## Tips
- **Start with a preset.** The Quick Setup dropdown covers most common use cases.
- **Use the preview to verify** before publishing.
- **Choose the right item type.** Text for metadata, Image for galleries, URL/Link for clickable terms.
- **Use inside a Post Context or Query Loop** for automatic context inheritance.

## Example uses
- displaying the current post's publish date
- listing all categories or tags for a post
- showing a custom field like a subtitle or external URL
- outputting a list of taxonomy terms as clickable links
- displaying an author's name, bio, and avatar in a template

