# Post Context block

The Post Context block is like a simpler Query Loop — but for a single post. You wrap a group of dynamic blocks inside it, pick one post, and every child block reads from that post automatically.

## Why it's useful

Each dynamic block already lets you pick a specific post using the **Post source** setting. But if you later want to point that card at a different post, you'd need to update every block one by one. With Post Context, you set the post **once** in the wrapper, and all child blocks follow.

## How it works

When you select a post, the block provides that post's ID and type as **context** to every child block. Any TMS block that supports dynamic content will automatically read from the selected post instead of the current page.

If no post is selected, the block outputs nothing at all.

## Settings sidebar

The settings sidebar has two tabs:

- **Wrapper** — Post selection and attributes
- **Styles** — Visual appearance of the wrapper element (see The Styles tab)

### Wrapper tab

#### Post Type
Choose the type of content — posts, pages, or any custom post type. Changing the post type resets the selected post.

#### Post Selector
Search and select a specific post. For attachment post types, becomes a media picker.

#### Element Tag
Same semantic tag options as the TMS Block: `div`, `section`, `article`, `header`, `footer`, `aside`, `nav`, `main`, `figure`.

#### ARIA Controls, Custom Attributes, Identity Controls
Same pattern as other blocks.

## Example HTML output

```html
<div class="tmsblocks-post-context tmsblocks-post-context-abc789 related-card">
  <h2 class="tmsblocks-heading tmsblocks-heading-def456">Getting Started with TMS Blocks</h2>
  <p class="tmsblocks-paragraph tmsblocks-paragraph-ghi123">Learn how to build clean, structured content…</p>
  <a href="https://example.com/getting-started" class="tmsblocks-anchor tmsblocks-anchor-jkl012">
    <span>Read more</span>
  </a>
</div>
```

## Tips
- **Set the post once, not per block.** One change updates everything inside.
- **Build reusable card patterns.** Copy the whole thing and just change the selected post.
- **Use `figure` as the wrapper tag for image/caption cards.**
- **No post selected = nothing shown.** Make sure to pick a post before publishing.

## Example uses
- a featured post card pointing to a hand-picked article
- a figure/img/caption pattern
- a set of post cards, each in its own Post Context
- a reusable card template — build once, duplicate, and repoint each copy

